  "narrative": {
    "northStar": "Clear as a bank statement, kind as a conversation",
    "overview": "Implemented 30 October 2026 from the approved banking concept ([PLAN.md](PLAN.md#approved-visual-concept)) and the [icon and chart specification](design/concepts/banking/ICON-AND-CHART-DIRECTION.md). Source of truth: `src/constants/theme.ts`, `src/components/ui/` and `src/features/categories/visual.ts`. Synthetic web previews were compared with the concept images; installed iOS/Android acceptance is still open (BR10).\n\n**North star: \"Clear as a bank statement, kind as a conversation.\"** White and cool-grey surfaces, one navy summary per screen, blue for actions, colour reserved for icon tiles and data graphics. Headings, amounts and paragraphs stay dark and readable.\n\n- Three tabs: Overview · Plan · Personal. Settings opens from the profile button (gear on Personal).\n- One navy summary per main screen; compact rows with fine dividers; grey bands separate row groups.\n- Shared and Personal share one visual system. Scope is stated in words (\"Shared\", \"Personal\", \"Visible to both of you\", \"Purchases are private\") — the earlier violet Private palette is retired. `Palettes.private` remains as an alias for existing `SpaceContext` callers.",
    "keyCharacteristics": [
      "Three tabs: Overview, Plan, Personal; Settings behind the profile button.",
      "One navy summary per main screen, compact rows, grey group bands.",
      "Colour only in icon tiles and data graphics, mapped by stable category identity.",
      "Scope, over-plan, refunds and estimates stated in words."
    ],
    "rules": [
      {
        "name": "The Honest Number Rule",
        "body": "Never call a figure a bank balance; unavailable is never shown as zero.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Identity Rule",
        "body": "Colour follows category ID or starter key, never list position or status.",
        "section": "colors"
